{"page_content": "If no specific information on Kp in marine water is available, Kpsusp,seawater ANd KPsed,seawater CAN be set equal to KPpsusp,freshwater ANG KPsed,freshwater, Fespectively.\n\nKp is expressed as the concentration of the substance sorbed to solids (in Mgchem:kQsolid*) divided by the concentration dissolved in porewater (Mdchem\u2018lwater +). The dimensionless form of Kp, or the total compartment-water partitioning coefficient in (mMg:Mcomp?)/(Mg:Mwater?), can\n\n49 The available QSARs in SimpleTreat 4 estimate log Koc in sewage sludge for ionisable substances on the basis of Log Dow. The Dow considers the solubility of the charged and neutral species in pure water and octanol at a specific pH and octanol is used as the surrogate for the soil matrix and all molecular interactions. Furthermore, for ionisable substances, octanol:water is not a good surrogate for the soil matrix, as octanol does not contain charged groups. As neither the pH dependence nor the ionic interactions between the solute and the soil matrix are accounted for in this approach the use of DOW approach may be followed with caution (Sigmund et al., 2022).\n\nbe derived from the definition of the soil in three phases:\n\n_ Ctotal comp K comp-water Cporew comp\n\nKD com Equation R.16-8 K comp-water _ Fair comp * K air-water + Fwater comp + F solid comp \u00b0 ee RHOsolid 1000\n\nwith comp \u20ac {soil , susp , sed}\n\nExplanation of symbols", "metadata": {"doc_id": "e41c49c9-51be-4480-8f47-afa9c7c9f363", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "IR_CSR_R16_V4_FINAL.pdf"}}